\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces SciForge system framework. The architecture organizes the workbench into user interaction and collaboration, research capability patterns, Core Engine, Scientific Model Router, and Infrastructure layers. User requests flow from desktop, group, and mobile surfaces into the Agent Runtime, which coordinates contextual research workflows, workflow automation, scientific modality routing, multimodal evidence generation, Evidence-DAG audit runs, and local-first infrastructure services.}}{8}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sciforge_framework}{{1}{8}{SciForge system framework. The architecture organizes the workbench into user interaction and collaboration, research capability patterns, Core Engine, Scientific Model Router, and Infrastructure layers. User requests flow from desktop, group, and mobile surfaces into the Agent Runtime, which coordinates contextual research workflows, workflow automation, scientific modality routing, multimodal evidence generation, Evidence-DAG audit runs, and local-first infrastructure services}{figure.1}{}}
